    "table csv": "Sample no.,Molar composition SiO2/GeO2,Molar composition MeO,Molar composition H2O,Molar composition TMHDA,Molar composition HF,Molar composition Products\n1,1:1,0,15-90,63.2,4,Amorphous\n2,1:1,0,105-120,63.2,4,ITH and amorphous\n3,0.8:1,0,15-120,101.1,4,Amorphous\n4,0.8:1,0,15-60,37.4,3,Amorphous\n5,0.8:1,0,75-120,37.4,3,ITH\n6,0.8:0,0,90,37.4,3,Amorphous\n7,1:(0.1-1),0,90,37.4,3,ITH\n8,1:0.4,0,90-120,28.0-37.4,3,ITH\n9,1:0.5,0.05,90,37.4,3,Cu-ITH and amorphous\n10,1:0.5,0.10,90,37.4,3,Cu-ITH\n11,1:0.5,0.15,90,37.4,3,Cu-ITH and amorphous\n12,1:0.5,0.20,90,37.4,3,Cu-ITH and amorphous\n13,1:0.5,0.05,90,37.4,3,Co-ITH and amorphous\n14,1:0.5,0.10,90,37.4,3,Co-ITH and amorphous\n15,1:0.5,0.15,90,37.4,3,Co-ITH\n16,1:0.5,0.20,90,37.4,3,Co-ITH",
    
    "extracted text": "The ITH-zeotype germanosilicates were synthesized under hydrothermal conditions using TMHDA as an OSDA. In a typical synthesis, 4 mL of TMHDA and 0.0262 g GeO2 were added to 0.81 mL water. The mixture was stirred using a magnetic stirrer until the germanium oxide was dissolved. After adding 0.1 mL of TEOS, the mixture was stirred for 30 min at room temperature to hydrolyze the TEOS, followed by the addition of 0.057 mL of an aqueous HF solution. The molar ratio of the batch composition was 0.5GeO2: 1SiO2:37.4OSDA:3HF:90H2O. The final mixture (pH 7-8) was sealed in a 25-mL Teflon-lined autoclave and heated to 170 °C under autogenous pressure for 7 days. For the synthesis of Co- and Cu-containing ITH, CoCl2·6H2O and CuCl2·2H2O were used as the precursors, respectively, and added into the reaction gel to obtain the following molar composition: 0.5GeO2:1SiO2:37.4OSDA:3HF:90H2O:0.15CoO or 0.10 CuO. All samples were synthesized at 170 °C for 7 days.",
    
    "property mapping": "SiO2 → Si\nGeO2 → Ge\nMeO → Cu or Co depending on the sample\nH2O → H2O\nTMHDA → osda_names (N,N,N',N'-tetramethyl-1,6-hexanediamine)\nHF → HF\nProducts → product_names\nCrystallization temperature: 170 °C\nCrystallization time: 7 days (168 hours)",
    
    "formula abbreviations": "TMHDA = N,N,N',N'-tetramethyl-1,6-hexanediamine (the organic structure-directing agent)\nMeO = Metal oxide, referring to either CuO or CoO depending on the sample\nTEOS = Tetraethyl orthosilicate (the silicon source)",
    
